 @kylejohnson6775  "They've been saying "we're fighting NATO" for years."

Yes, they have... but they haven't convinced the average Alexander of a need to mobilize... an actual war with NATO could change that.

I believe that breaking up NATO is indeed a long-term goal of Russia, but not the driver behind the current situation.

 @Volkbrecht  Drop Ukraine? You made me laugh thats for sure.
Yeah no, even if the European Union "Dropped Ukraine", the Ukrainians would not just lose the war in weeks- thats A russian thinking.
I mean, just look at what the Ukrainian domestic drone industry has done to Russia. Those Ukrainian drones hitting Russian refineries, causing an oil crisis in a major oil producer, them also closing the Russian airspace, bombing generals in Russia- thats got nothing to do with Europe at all. Thats just the Ukrainians. People really undervalue how far a nation will fight to survive, and given that Russia has lost a million men in a war thats taken four years, even without European support, this will drag along even longer.

